{"type":"message","id":"c2cb1a1c","parentId":"8f37fa0a","timestamp":"2026-02-18T09:44:39.817Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-02-18 15:14 GMT+5:30] URGENT FORENSIC DIAGNOSIS: OpenClaw gateway refuses to stay running after restart or start. It immediately crashes. Need to find root cause and fix.\n\n**Investigation plan:**\n\n1. **Check installation integrity:**\n   - Run `openclaw version` and `openclaw doctor --verbose` to see any hidden errors\n   - Verify all required binaries exist in the installation directory\n   - Check for missing DLLs or dependencies (especially on Windows)\n\n2. **Examine configuration file:**\n   - Validate JSON syntax (no trailing commas, proper escaping)\n   - Look for non-ASCII characters or encoding issues in `openclaw.json`\n   - Check if any paths contain special characters or spaces that might break parsing\n   - Temporarily replace with a known-good minimal config to see if that starts\n\n3. **Review gateway startup sequence:**\n   - Identify where it might panic: config loading, plugin initialization, model catalog loading, network binding, agent creation\n   - Check if port 18789 is already in use by another process (even a zombie)\n   - Look for file permission issues on `.openclaw-state/` directory\n   - Verify that the `openclaw` command is being run from the correct working directory\n\n4. **Signal handling on Windows:**\n   - `restart` sends SIGUSR1; on Windows this may be implemented via an event or named pipe. Check if the signal handler is registered correctly.\n   - Could be that the restart logic calls `os.Exit` prematurely before the new process is ready.\n   - Look for race conditions: old process kills itself before new process starts listening.\n\n5. **Logging:**\n   - Enable maximum logging: set `logging.consoleLevel` to `trace` and run in foreground with `--debug --no-daemon` to capture output to console.\n   - Redirect output to a file: `openclaw gateway --debug --no-daemon 2>&1 | tee gateway-debug.log`\n   - Capture any panic stack traces or error messages.\n\n6. **Compare working vs broken states:**\n   - Does `openclaw gateway start` ever work? If yes, what's different about `restart`?\n   - Try starting with `--no-daemon` manually; does it stay up?\n   - Check if the gateway PID is written to a file and maybe causing lock contention.\n\n7. **Check for known issues:**\n   - Search GitHub issues for \"restart crash windows\" or \"gateway exits immediately\"\n   - Look at code in `gateway/restart.go`, `gateway/main.go`, `gateway/signal.go` (if exists)\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Exact error message or panic stack trace from running in debug foreground\n- Identification of the failing component (config, plugin, signal handler, etc.)\n- Concrete fix: either a code patch (diff) or a configuration change that resolves it\n- If it's an OpenClaw bug, provide a minimal reproducible example and suggest a temporary workaround script\n- Write findings to `gateway-crash-forensic-report.md` in workspace root\n\n**Important:** Use direct commands to reproduce: `openclaw gateway --debug --no-daemon` and capture the output. Do not rely on `restart` until we know why it crashes.\n\nRun this on the host (not in a subagent loop that might time out). Keep the gateway process running in foreground so we can see the error.\n\nStart now and report back within 30 minutes with the first error capture."}],"timestamp":1771407879812}}
